54Z","closed_at":"2025-12-29T13:40:48Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.6.beta (63227bbc8)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.beta (63227bbc8) - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8180) - AMD Ryzen 7 7800X3D 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 63.11 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen editing a previously opened but now closed file through `Find in Files` the changes do not show up when the file is opened in the editor, but show up in external editors.\n\nFrom what I can tell this comes from editing the files directly on disk, which causes some cache to not update. Maybe there is a way to update the affected cache manually.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. create a new project\n2. create a new GDScript file\n3. add any tex to the scriptt (it will be replaced later) and save it\n4. close the file in the editor\n5. press `Ctrl+Shift+F` to open `Find in Files`\n6. search for something present in the closed file and use `Replace` to replace it with something else\n7. open the file in the internal editor and the changes should not appear\n8. open the file in an external editor where the changes should be visible\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNot project specific","closed_by":{"login":"TheDying0fLight","id":95179191,"node_id":"U_kgDOBaxRtw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95179191?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight","html_url":"https://github.com/TheDying0fLight","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight